From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Aring <aahringo@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2020 20:04:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fs: dlm: flush othercon at close

This patch ensures we also flush the othercon writequeue when a lowcomms
close occurs.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Aring <aahringo@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: David Teigland <teigland@redhat.com>
---
 fs/dlm/lowcomms.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/dlm/lowcomms.c b/fs/dlm/lowcomms.c
index 395f4b693e80..fbcd5aeb8cfb 100644
--- a/fs/dlm/lowcomms.c
+++ b/fs/dlm/lowcomms.c
@@ -1517,6 +1517,8 @@ int dlm_lowcomms_close(int nodeid)
 		set_bit(CF_CLOSE, &con->flags);
 		close_connection(con, true, true, true);
 		clean_one_writequeue(con);
+		if (con->othercon)
+			clean_one_writequeue(con->othercon);
 	}
 
 	spin_lock(&dlm_node_addrs_spin);
